abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program. This v0.5 chapter disassembles time into four independent finite theorems: the time fiber is a torsor (fully lawful, no derivable origin — the origin is a received selection priced by the v0.3 selector debt); law-time covers visible-time (a cyclic visible dynamics lifts uniquely to an ascending helix with conserved monodromy); an arrow of time needs no thermodynamics (a reversible dynamics coupled to a question ledger never returns jointly — exhaustively verified); and lawfulness needs no foundation (guarded self-reference has unique base-case-free solutions, and a Mobius-twisted cover has perfect local time with no global now). All results are machine-checked by a shipped dependency-free script; earlier chapters are unchanged and every unearned generalization is held open by name."
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-07-13"
